#
# Conformance case: teleology/iteration-zero-pass.
#
# A logic:Iteration whose logic:iterationCondition is false at the start state runs ZERO body passes and still succeeds: the outcome records logic:transactionSucceeds true with a single-state path (no logic:temporallySucceeds edges, no step substrate). Proves the zero-iteration boundary.
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom the
# projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/iteration-zero-pass/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
